2026-10-09T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2307) 'XR Pilot keeps the runtime's PyroWave packets as they arrive and a separate step decodes them on an idle GPU into a CineForm intermediate
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2307) 'XR Pilot and its MCP server, the pyro2cfhd and frames2cfhd tools, the CineForm SDK build, and the av1mkv delivery of a recording
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2307) 'A recording keeps the runtime's own video stream and encodes it later on an idle GPU.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Encoding live on the VR GPU would compete with the compositor, which an overload had already killed twice that day.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2307) 'The shared desk is run as the open work below records.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2307) 'recording the xr pilot stream to cineform
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2307) 'A recording is the runtime's own video stream, not a screen capture. The pilot appends each PyroWave packet to a `.pwrec` file with its presentation and receive times and does no encoding while VR runs. A one-shot job later decodes the packets on the GPU that is not driving VR and encodes CineForm on the CPU. The CineForm file is the intermediate the delivery step wraps as MKV with a `.cff` (operator, 2026-10-09).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2307) '- RFD66606-2303, the XR requirements; RFD66606-2365, the recording rules.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2307) '- RFD66606-2306, operating the shared desk; RFD66606-2302, the frame budget.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Superseded by nut-based ffmpeg recording
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Recording moved to nut-based ffmpeg and works, so this RFD is committed (operator, 2026-11-11). The `.pwrec` and CineForm steps below are the earlier design and stay as history.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2307) 'The packet file
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2307) '`.pwrec` starts with the magic `PWREC`, two zero bytes and a version byte. Each frame is a u64 presentation time in ns, a u64 receive time in ns, a u32 index, a u32 byte count and the payload, at most 256 MiB. A pilot that restarts writes the next file with `.1.pwrec`. `xr-pilot --record-stream` and the MCP server's `--record-stream <out>` write it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2307) 'The decode step
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2307) '`pyro2cfhd <in.pwrec> <out.cfhd>` takes `--fps`, `--size`, `--quality` and `--gpu` (a PCI vendor and device pair). It runs as a one-shot task on the GPU without VR. `frames2cfhd` does the same from PNG frames. Both share one fit and RIFF writer.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2307) '- The CineForm RIFF file stops at 4 GB.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2307) '- The MKV writer built with llvm-mingw fails past 2 GB.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2307) '- Full-rate 4K therefore needs a container writer fix before it ships.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Building CineForm with MSVC
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Two changes let the CineForm SDK build with MSVC on the desk: `simd_compat.h` includes `malloc.h` for the aligned allocators, which MSVC has in place of `mm_malloc.h`; `lutpath.cpp` declares its registry value name `LPCTSTR`, so string literals assign to it under strict strings. The llvm-mingw build of av1mkv needs the toolchain's libc++ and libunwind DLLs beside it, or it exits with 0xc00004bc.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Motion that does not stutter
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Walking was integrated in the 60 Hz window loop while the tracking sender ran at a fixed 90 Hz, so one packet in three repeated a pose. The sender now runs at the runtime's announced refresh rate, clamped to 60 to 144 Hz, and moves held keys by real elapsed time; the window applies mouse look only. The wheel scales walk speed by 1.25 per notch, from 0.25 to 8 m/s; with Shift it moves the hand's reach. A 3D head gizmo draws yaw and pitch as arcs, so a trace shows when the head looks straight up or down.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2307) 'Open work
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2307) '- Run the `pyro2cfhd` self-test on the desk's second GPU, then record a real two-minute stream and deliver it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2307) '- Count compositor sync timeouts in the driver and give the sparklines fault thresholds, set from the sweep this RFD records.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2307) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-09T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2307) 'The first two-minute sweep was saved as left-eye PNG frames and encoded at 10 fps, because a full-rate 4K clip passes the size limits of the CineForm RIFF writer and of the MKV writer built with llvm-mingw.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2307  1 LINE
 Text:Written
